From 8a92d551c7f95e0447e6114e1bef657eda51d788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KD9TAW <kd9taw@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:50:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: sat uplink sideband mirror iteration - reverted
 approach, NOT for main

Preserved from an uncommitted worktree found while reconciling local work,
so a worktree cleanup cannot destroy it. The reconciliation review found this
iteration in no commit on any ref: the doppler.rs ruling that CW does not mirror
and why, the PKTUSB<->PKTLSB and RTTY<->RTTYR mirror table, the CI-V
civ_mode_and_data resolver in broker.rs, and the tests
an_inverting_bird_puts_the_mirrored_side_on_the_wire_in_every_section and
a_pile_up_split_worked_after_a_pass_states_its_own_mode.

The merged approach was reverted on main in 5071e64a (2026-08-03). This is
groundwork for a later attempt, not a fix. Any revival is a hard-gated transmit
change and needs bench verification on real hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xxa5mYyWRrK4DQZpVYsAMd
